Spec: Pen Tool

Purpose:
  Create Bézier paths by placing anchor points with optional control handles.

Owns:
  ./pen.ts
  ./pen.test.ts

Must:
  Click places a corner node (straight segment).
  Click+drag places a smooth node (curved segment with tangent handles).
  Shift constrains new segments to 45° increments.
  Clicking the first node closes the path.
  Enter or Escape finishes as an open path.
  Preview line shows from last node to cursor during drawing.
  Snap to existing endpoints/midpoints when enabled.
  Created path is pushed to store via CreateShapeCommand.

Must not:
  Modify existing shapes.
  Create zero-length paths (discard if only one node placed).
  Leave the path in an uncommitted state after tool switch.

Depends on:
  @BaseTool
  @PathShape
  @PathNode
  @CreateShapeCommand
  @SnapManager

Scenario: draw triangle
  Given the Pen tool is active
  When the user clicks at 3 positions and closes the path
  Then a closed PathShape with 3 corner nodes exists
  And it is the selected shape

Tasks:
  [x] Click to place corner nodes.
  [x] Click+drag for smooth nodes.
  [x] Close path by clicking first node.
  [x] Finish open path with Enter/Escape.
  [x] Preview line rendering.
  [x] Shift constraint for 45° angles.
  [x] Integration with snap system.
